WEBVTT

00:12.095 --> 00:14.347
- [lights clunk]
- [phone chimes]

00:14.431 --> 00:17.016
[announcer]
Please wait until the game commences.

00:17.100 --> 00:20.395
Five minutes
until game registration closes.

00:20.478 --> 00:22.480
[carnival music playing]

00:22.564 --> 00:24.649
[Sagano] This time it's a Ferris wheel.

00:26.568 --> 00:28.611
Wonder what kind of game it is, huh?

00:30.864 --> 00:33.074
Tonight, our visas will expire.

00:34.492 --> 00:35.744
[sighs]

00:35.827 --> 00:37.328
We have to play it.

00:39.372 --> 00:41.374
[Arisu] Um, can I bother you for a sec?

00:43.668 --> 00:47.172
Have you… Have you
ever heard of the Beach?

00:47.756 --> 00:48.715
What?

00:49.257 --> 00:51.426
- [Sagano] Leave him alone, let's go.
- [Arisu] Wait!

00:51.509 --> 00:54.471
[Aibara screams]

01:06.566 --> 01:08.485
Where the hell is this Beach?

01:08.568 --> 01:11.071
[announcer] Registration is now closed.

01:11.154 --> 01:12.989
The game will now commence.

01:16.117 --> 01:18.119
[theme music]

02:26.354 --> 02:28.481
[Usagi]
We still don't know where the Beach is.

02:30.024 --> 02:32.318
[Arisu] And now, we're back here again.

02:37.740 --> 02:39.492
[crickets chirping]

02:39.576 --> 02:43.163
If we don't join up in a game soon,
our visas will expire.

02:51.045 --> 02:52.046
[sighs]

02:53.423 --> 02:55.425
My visa expires in three days.

02:58.303 --> 02:59.470
[exhales deeply]

03:02.223 --> 03:03.391
Three days to go.

03:04.976 --> 03:06.853
But I'll find that Beach and…

03:08.229 --> 03:10.273
I'll put an end to this damn game.

03:18.907 --> 03:21.451
[Usagi] Tomorrow, I'll do a day hunt.
Wanna come with me?

03:22.702 --> 03:24.203
[Arisu] Is that okay?

03:24.287 --> 03:26.956
Can't promise I'll stay out of your way,
but I'll do my best.

03:28.583 --> 03:31.878
All the knowledge
that you've discovered about nature…

03:32.837 --> 03:35.214
I need to learn, and learn right away.

03:38.051 --> 03:40.011
Life comes with consequence.

03:41.721 --> 03:44.182
Without thinking about that,
somehow I've lived till now.

03:46.059 --> 03:48.436
[inhales sharply]
Those guys trusted me.

03:49.437 --> 03:51.105
They died believing in me.

03:53.608 --> 03:56.027
I may also die soon, and for what?

03:57.612 --> 03:58.821
For now…
[exhales sharply]

04:00.073 --> 04:02.450
I don't want to waste
even a single minute, not a second.

04:08.539 --> 04:09.749
Have a good night.

04:25.390 --> 04:27.600
[breathes deeply]

04:28.643 --> 04:30.103
[exhales deeply]

04:30.186 --> 04:32.188
[sentimental music]

04:37.402 --> 04:38.403
[exhales deeply]

04:38.903 --> 04:40.780
Without the city lights hiding them…

04:42.323 --> 04:44.200
the stars look beautiful.

04:54.252 --> 04:56.879
[mosquito buzzing]

04:56.963 --> 04:58.172
[slaps]

04:58.256 --> 04:59.799
Damn!
[grumbles]

05:01.426 --> 05:02.343
[grunts]

05:03.469 --> 05:04.554
Damn it!

05:05.138 --> 05:06.264
[groans]

05:08.391 --> 05:10.935
[Usagi] I told you not to stay out there.

05:12.270 --> 05:14.397
It's okay, you can sleep in the tent.

05:15.189 --> 05:17.692
But… but, uh…

05:20.903 --> 05:23.156
Your worst enemy's lack of sleep.

05:23.239 --> 05:27.160
Being alert and totally rested can make
the difference between life and death.

05:28.286 --> 05:30.079
[mosquito buzzing]

05:45.928 --> 05:47.847
[inhales deeply]

05:47.930 --> 05:49.932
[upbeat music]

05:59.400 --> 06:00.902
[Usagi] Clearly, wild boars live here.

06:00.985 --> 06:04.280
This is a mud puddle.
It's where the boars bathe themselves.

06:04.906 --> 06:06.157
I also noticed…

06:07.241 --> 06:10.119
that dug up soil
where they forage for leaf buds.

06:10.620 --> 06:12.497
Sharpen their claws on the tree stump.

06:13.831 --> 06:15.541
There are wild boars in Odaiba?

06:16.626 --> 06:20.088
The humans are gone,
so the animals came back to the city.

06:23.382 --> 06:25.760
Rule one of hunting is
to look for footprints.

06:27.386 --> 06:29.555
The boundary lines
of an animal's territory

06:29.639 --> 06:31.224
spreads out in a mesh pattern.

06:33.434 --> 06:36.479
To hunt, all you need to do is
connect those lines.

06:37.063 --> 06:39.941
Then you'll know
the comings and goings of your prey.

06:41.025 --> 06:45.780
In other words, know their playing field,
connect the lines.

06:46.697 --> 06:47.949
You learn quickly.

06:48.533 --> 06:50.535
The video game Battleland follows
the same idea.

06:51.369 --> 06:52.286
Battleland?

06:52.870 --> 06:54.413
[Arisu] Yeah, it's an online game.

06:55.206 --> 06:56.165
Online game?

06:56.874 --> 06:58.084
You can play it online.

06:59.085 --> 07:00.086
Huh.

07:04.715 --> 07:06.717
[ominous music]

07:16.269 --> 07:17.979
[Usagi on radio] What do you see?

07:18.855 --> 07:21.023
There are about ten participants
in the game.

07:21.107 --> 07:24.735
Don't know what's going on.
They seem to be forming a team.

07:24.819 --> 07:25.862
What about you?

07:25.945 --> 07:29.365
I see four people. I'll pretend
I'm joining the game and talk to them.

07:30.450 --> 07:31.451
[Arisu] Hey, wait a second.

07:32.869 --> 07:35.288
- What?
- Look at the participants' wrists.

07:35.371 --> 07:36.747
[Usagi] Their wrists?

07:36.831 --> 07:38.207
Any of yours wearing a locker key?

07:38.791 --> 07:40.918
Like the ones you get in a fitness club.

07:43.087 --> 07:45.047
I saw them when we were playing tag.

07:45.965 --> 07:47.008
Here it is.

07:51.637 --> 07:53.347
They must've been on a team.

07:54.098 --> 07:55.475
Wait, I see…

07:56.559 --> 07:58.436
[gasps]
I see two wearing them.

07:58.519 --> 08:00.271
Keep your eye on them.

08:01.063 --> 08:02.148
[Usagi] Got it.

08:02.231 --> 08:04.233
[foreboding music]

08:05.776 --> 08:08.905
[explosions]

08:12.408 --> 08:14.285
[Arisu]
The ones who cleared the game came out.

08:14.368 --> 08:16.162
I was right. They have locker keys.

08:16.245 --> 08:19.165
[Usagi] Over here, three people came out.
They split up and walked off.

08:19.248 --> 08:21.667
Two of them had locker keys,
they seem like they're together.

08:21.751 --> 08:24.295
They're headed in the same direction.
I'll follow them.

08:25.546 --> 08:27.465
[men whooping, laughing]

08:27.548 --> 08:28.674
- It's over!
- Yeah!

08:28.758 --> 08:30.551
- Let's go back.
- [man 1] Let's get out of here!

08:30.635 --> 08:32.428
- [men laughing]
- [man 2] Yeah, let's go!

08:39.101 --> 08:40.186
[whispering]
Usagi.

08:40.978 --> 08:42.605
[Usagi] Did you see that too?

08:42.688 --> 08:44.398
It's definitely these guys.

08:45.233 --> 08:48.027
[man 3] I knew we were gonna win!
Come on, let's go!

08:48.110 --> 08:49.654
[engine revs]

08:49.737 --> 08:51.614
[Usagi] They're getting into a car.

08:51.697 --> 08:53.407
[Arisu] They might be collecting
all these old cars

08:53.491 --> 08:54.951
as an organization.

08:57.078 --> 08:58.329
They're rolling!

08:58.412 --> 08:59.956
[Usagi] Mine are too!

09:00.039 --> 09:01.958
[Usagi panting]

09:02.542 --> 09:04.293
[tires squeal]

09:05.545 --> 09:07.505
[Arisu] The car's headed for Maihama!

09:07.588 --> 09:08.714
[Usagi] Mine too!

09:09.215 --> 09:11.842
[intense electronic music]

09:15.096 --> 09:17.640
[panting]

09:25.898 --> 09:28.818
[intense electronic music continues]

09:29.735 --> 09:31.612
[engine revs louder]

09:35.366 --> 09:37.660
[panting echoes]

09:38.744 --> 09:41.247
[upbeat music playing in distance]

09:44.917 --> 09:45.918
[Usagi] Is that it?

09:52.508 --> 09:53.509
BEACH

09:53.593 --> 09:54.594
[Arisu] "Beach."

09:56.137 --> 09:57.054
That's it.

09:57.972 --> 09:59.515
How does it have electricity?

10:01.392 --> 10:03.853
Will we find the answers
to our questions there?

10:06.689 --> 10:07.690
- [gasps]
- [thwacks]

10:13.321 --> 10:14.280
[exhales heavily]

10:19.160 --> 10:20.369
[Mira] Good morning.

10:21.412 --> 10:23.706
I apologize for this rude introduction.

10:24.540 --> 10:27.960
Our sentries report
that there were people spying on us.

10:28.753 --> 10:30.296
Why are you here?

10:34.800 --> 10:36.010
I was told that…

10:36.594 --> 10:38.429
I could find answers here.

10:39.847 --> 10:41.432
What is this game?

10:42.933 --> 10:44.769
And where is everybody?

10:47.730 --> 10:48.939
[door opens]

10:49.815 --> 10:51.150
Where indeed.

10:52.443 --> 10:55.863
We have the answers
that you are looking for.

10:55.946 --> 10:57.239
[door closes]

11:02.244 --> 11:03.496
Welcome…

11:04.955 --> 11:07.750
to the oasis known as the Beach.

11:11.587 --> 11:13.589
[laughs]

11:15.007 --> 11:17.885
Here is the first answer.

11:17.968 --> 11:18.844
[snaps]

11:21.806 --> 11:23.808
[suspenseful music]

11:25.684 --> 11:28.020
[door rattling]

11:37.822 --> 11:39.824
[suspenseful music continues]

11:51.377 --> 11:53.462
[Hatter] Allow me to enlighten you.

11:54.505 --> 11:56.132
These cards…

11:56.215 --> 11:59.844
These cards are the only way
to end your nightmare.

12:00.719 --> 12:05.641
To clear the game,
you must collect all the cards.

12:07.435 --> 12:09.270
Collect all of the cards?

12:10.896 --> 12:12.690
If we collect all of the cards,

12:13.524 --> 12:15.776
will the world we once knew return?

12:19.822 --> 12:21.907
It's not the world that will return.

12:22.867 --> 12:24.535
Only one person…

12:25.119 --> 12:27.413
can return to the normal world.

12:28.622 --> 12:29.790
Huh?

12:30.791 --> 12:31.709
Only one?

12:34.587 --> 12:37.882
It's impossible for one person
to clear all the games

12:37.965 --> 12:40.134
and collect all 52 cards.

12:40.885 --> 12:42.636
They could not do this alone.

12:43.345 --> 12:44.638
That's suicide.

12:45.306 --> 12:47.850
That's why we've united as one

12:48.559 --> 12:50.978
in order to allow one person to leave.

12:51.645 --> 12:54.315
That is the Beach's objective.

12:55.483 --> 13:00.279
[Hatter] You have been given good cards,
I've been told.

13:01.155 --> 13:05.284
From now on, let's play together.
United, as one,

13:05.367 --> 13:08.037
and collect the remaining cards together.

13:10.164 --> 13:11.290
If we say no?

13:11.874 --> 13:14.168
You can't say no.

13:16.128 --> 13:17.671
Your visa…

13:18.214 --> 13:19.840
expires today.

13:21.842 --> 13:24.595
Seems like you have to join us, yeah?

13:27.056 --> 13:29.433
If we help you,
you're saying we can end the game?

13:30.976 --> 13:32.186
Will this be over?

13:33.562 --> 13:35.564
Can't answer that for certain.

13:35.648 --> 13:38.442
But there are indications
that it's possible.

13:40.236 --> 13:44.698
Everyone in this room,
long before you entered the game,

13:45.324 --> 13:47.785
has been searching this country.

13:48.577 --> 13:51.497
What do you mean… this "country"?

13:52.456 --> 13:56.168
Visas have been issued, therefore,

13:57.044 --> 13:58.671
this is a country.

14:00.965 --> 14:04.760
It seems that the people of Tokyo
haven't all disappeared like we have.

14:05.594 --> 14:06.679
We wonder,

14:07.304 --> 14:10.724
have we been transported somehow
to another country?

14:11.392 --> 14:12.685
If we have,

14:13.394 --> 14:15.604
there must be a way to return.

14:16.605 --> 14:21.735
So together, all of us built
this small organization.

14:21.819 --> 14:25.114
Electricity is produced
from a fuel-powered generator.

14:25.656 --> 14:27.908
We use rainwater for our water supply.

14:28.617 --> 14:31.328
We got our firearms
from the living and the dead.

14:32.329 --> 14:36.417
[Hatter] However, only a select few of us
are allowed to use them.

14:38.168 --> 14:42.047
Our aim here is to unite and collect
all the cards together.

14:43.257 --> 14:44.550
And in this…

14:45.175 --> 14:47.303
paradise, this Beach,

14:47.386 --> 14:50.055
we only have three rules.

14:50.681 --> 14:51.932
Rule one.

14:52.558 --> 14:55.060
Always wear a swimsuit wherever you go.

14:56.353 --> 14:57.229
Why?

14:57.313 --> 14:58.314
[chuckles]

14:58.939 --> 15:03.068
You can't conceal a weapon in a swimsuit,
so it's safe.

15:03.861 --> 15:05.321
Also, here,

15:05.404 --> 15:08.866
you are free to drown in alcohol,
get high on drugs,

15:08.949 --> 15:10.576
and have sex as much as you want.

15:12.077 --> 15:15.164
Enjoy your life while you still can.

15:16.123 --> 15:20.169
All keys and locks
have been destroyed and thrown away.

15:20.252 --> 15:22.212
There are no secrets.

15:23.172 --> 15:24.381
Rule two.

15:25.090 --> 15:28.260
All cards are the Beach's property.

15:28.969 --> 15:32.348
That means that all the cards
you've collected,

15:32.431 --> 15:34.934
we'll hang onto for safekeeping.

15:37.478 --> 15:41.649
Those who have contributed their cards
will be promoted in numerical order.

15:42.566 --> 15:46.987
You see, after our collective effort
sends out the first person,

15:48.030 --> 15:52.493
it won't be long before we can gather
enough duplicate cards

15:52.576 --> 15:55.579
to send out a second person,
then a third, and so on.

15:57.206 --> 16:00.709
The day when the Beach's brothers
and sisters can leave this country

16:00.793 --> 16:02.419
is fast approaching.

16:05.839 --> 16:07.841
And when exactly will that be?

16:11.929 --> 16:13.055
What if…

16:14.139 --> 16:15.891
I refuse to join?

16:18.560 --> 16:20.562
[ominous music]

16:26.360 --> 16:28.570
Well, there's rule three.

16:30.739 --> 16:32.658
The last one.

16:35.953 --> 16:38.831
Death to all traitors.

16:38.914 --> 16:41.500
[ominous music continues]

16:46.755 --> 16:49.675
People in this room
have sacrificed everything

16:49.758 --> 16:54.430
to ensure a first departure
from the Beach one glorious day.

16:54.513 --> 16:57.683
Soldiers in a great cause!

17:00.769 --> 17:03.230
To those who plot against us…

17:04.189 --> 17:06.483
Beach shows no mercy.

17:07.317 --> 17:09.862
[ominous music continues]

17:28.380 --> 17:29.465
Usagi.

17:30.758 --> 17:31.633
I'm sorry…

17:33.510 --> 17:35.345
that I got you involved.

17:38.015 --> 17:39.224
Don't apologize.

17:40.893 --> 17:42.478
I wanted to be involved.

17:45.064 --> 17:46.815
I knew what I was doing.

17:50.778 --> 17:55.491
[Hatter whistling]

18:03.999 --> 18:05.667
[laughs]

18:07.127 --> 18:09.671
[laughing continues]

18:14.968 --> 18:16.762
The Seven of Hearts!

18:17.596 --> 18:19.723
The cards are with us!

18:21.016 --> 18:24.353
One of us is closer
to leaving this country.

18:24.436 --> 18:25.604
We thank you.

18:26.980 --> 18:31.568
Rest assured that we will consider
promoting the two of you.

18:32.486 --> 18:33.695
And now!

18:34.321 --> 18:37.449
Enjoy the Beach and whatever you desire.

18:38.826 --> 18:41.703
[suspenseful music intensifies]

18:41.787 --> 18:43.789
[upbeat techno music playing]

18:48.544 --> 18:50.754
[crowd chattering indistinctly]

18:58.095 --> 19:00.848
[crowd whooping, chattering]

19:09.189 --> 19:10.691
What the hell?

19:41.513 --> 19:42.598
I feel like…

19:43.390 --> 19:45.017
we're being watched.

19:46.143 --> 19:48.353
Newcomers are always
a spectacle to others.

19:54.193 --> 19:57.112
[upbeat techno music playing]

20:00.741 --> 20:04.036
[DJ] Yeah, let's get it going!

20:04.119 --> 20:07.456
Beach party! Get this blowout started!

20:08.916 --> 20:10.751
Come on!

20:10.834 --> 20:12.461
This is messed up.

20:12.544 --> 20:16.089
- Do you believe what we're seeing?
- [horn blaring]

20:16.173 --> 20:18.592
[shouts]
Hey, it's game time!

20:18.675 --> 20:21.511
[crowd cheering]

20:24.139 --> 20:27.893
A new game arena
has been confirmed in Shinagawa!

20:27.976 --> 20:30.896
- The cars are in the second parking lot!
- Adachi and Koto wards,

20:30.979 --> 20:32.481
form two groups! Let's go!

20:32.564 --> 20:33.732
[crowd cheering]

20:33.815 --> 20:38.278
Hatter! Hatter! Hatter!
Hatter! Hatter! Hatter!

20:38.362 --> 20:39.696
[cheering]

20:39.780 --> 20:43.617
Hatter! Hatter! Hatter!
Hatter! Hatter! Hatter!

20:49.248 --> 20:50.582
Comrades!

20:51.250 --> 20:53.252
Tonight brings us a new challenge.

20:54.753 --> 20:57.005
And my soldiers never back down from one.

20:57.839 --> 21:01.093
This challenge is a war
against your own fear.

21:01.176 --> 21:04.513
[Hatter] Individually, each of you
has the courage within to play.

21:04.596 --> 21:06.098
To battle and to win.

21:06.181 --> 21:08.350
And when you stand united as one,

21:08.976 --> 21:11.103
nothing can stand in your way.

21:12.396 --> 21:15.315
Together, we will get the cards we need

21:16.066 --> 21:18.110
to return us to our old world.

21:19.278 --> 21:20.112
I know

21:20.779 --> 21:22.322
that you will get there!

21:22.406 --> 21:24.741
[crowd cheering]

21:24.825 --> 21:25.993
Let's do it!

21:26.076 --> 21:29.037
[cheering continues]

21:29.621 --> 21:32.332
Go to the car that has your number!

21:33.792 --> 21:37.170
Is this what we are now? One of them?
Collecting cards?

21:37.963 --> 21:39.798
We've been divided
into two separate games.

21:41.091 --> 21:42.384
Promise me you'll be careful?

21:42.467 --> 21:46.096
[techno music playing]

21:48.181 --> 21:49.266
What's wrong?

21:50.767 --> 21:52.894
We were together in the last game.

21:54.354 --> 21:56.732
- Who? Those two?
- Yeah.

21:57.733 --> 21:59.109
Maybe we can use them.

21:59.609 --> 22:01.111
They could fit into the plan.

22:05.407 --> 22:07.534
[engines revving loudly]

22:07.617 --> 22:10.329
[man on radio] Team 1 to Team 9,
proceed to the game arena in Shinagawa.

22:10.412 --> 22:13.081
Team 10 to Team 17,
head to the game arena in Koto.

22:13.165 --> 22:15.292
Team 18 to 24, please proceed…

22:15.375 --> 22:18.211
[announcer] Game, "Jungle Beast Hunter".

22:18.295 --> 22:21.631
Work together to defeat the jungle beasts.

22:21.715 --> 22:24.926
Refer to the scoreboard for point value.

22:25.010 --> 22:27.804
[carnival music playing]

22:30.849 --> 22:32.559
- [roars]
- [screams]

22:34.061 --> 22:36.396
[roaring]

22:36.980 --> 22:39.316
- [announcer] Game, "Borrowed Time".
- [screaming]

22:39.900 --> 22:41.276
Hang on!

22:45.113 --> 22:47.157
[announcer] Game, "Human Elevator".

22:52.245 --> 22:55.457
[announcer]
Game, "Bingo Night at the Match Factory".

22:56.958 --> 22:59.086
Use the eight matches provided

22:59.586 --> 23:03.256
to collect the numbers hidden
in the 24 rooms.

23:03.340 --> 23:05.967
To clear the game, make a bingo.

23:07.677 --> 23:09.805
- [people screaming]
- Out of the way! Out of the way!

23:09.888 --> 23:11.973
[gunshots]

23:12.057 --> 23:13.517
WILD BOAR
50 POINTS RECEIVED

23:13.600 --> 23:14.643
EAGLE
30 POINTS RECEIVED

23:14.726 --> 23:17.229
[thrilling music]

23:19.731 --> 23:21.691
[grumbling]

23:23.318 --> 23:24.903
[screams]

23:24.986 --> 23:27.405
[breathing heavily]

23:29.991 --> 23:32.994
[tiger growling]

23:35.580 --> 23:36.540
[roars]

23:38.708 --> 23:40.293
- [gunshot]
- [roars]

23:41.753 --> 23:43.255
- [gunshot]
- [roars]

23:43.338 --> 23:45.841
[gunshots]

23:45.924 --> 23:47.968
- [grunts]
- [tiger groans]

23:48.051 --> 23:49.386
[alarm blaring]

23:49.469 --> 23:51.054
[pants]

23:52.097 --> 23:53.598
Where is it?

23:55.308 --> 23:58.770
[machine powers down]

23:58.854 --> 24:01.898
[breathes nervously, screams]

24:01.982 --> 24:03.733
[swooshing]

24:03.817 --> 24:06.153
[whoop, laughs]

24:06.236 --> 24:08.697
[gunshots]

24:08.780 --> 24:09.948
CROW
1 POINT RECEIVED

24:10.031 --> 24:11.741
Too easy!

24:14.286 --> 24:15.537
That's it.

24:16.163 --> 24:17.539
[Usagi] Room 4D is 9.

24:17.622 --> 24:20.000
[chiming]

24:20.083 --> 24:22.085
[suspenseful music]

24:27.299 --> 24:28.675
[roars]

24:37.893 --> 24:40.562
[water pattering]

24:59.664 --> 25:00.707
[scanner beeps]

25:02.542 --> 25:03.585
[beeps]

25:04.711 --> 25:06.713
[tense music]

25:10.884 --> 25:14.846
1 PER PERSON

25:18.516 --> 25:19.809
[phone chimes]

25:19.893 --> 25:22.020
This test will tell us
if you're a good candidate

25:22.103 --> 25:23.939
for a Beach executive post.

25:24.564 --> 25:26.399
So, do your best.

25:30.946 --> 25:31.905
[phone chimes]

25:32.656 --> 25:34.241
A waterproof cover?

25:36.326 --> 25:39.704
- [phone chimes]
- I'm Kuina. Good to meet ya.

25:40.997 --> 25:42.249
Me too.

25:43.041 --> 25:44.292
[Tatta] Ms. Ann!

25:44.876 --> 25:47.087
The water's coming out pretty fast,
it's getting deeper.

25:47.170 --> 25:50.590
[panting]
Hey, you!

25:52.384 --> 25:56.096
Wow, you played tag. You made it, huh?

25:56.179 --> 25:58.223
Yeah, now at the Beach, I'm a mechanic--

25:58.306 --> 26:00.308
You can talk when the game's over.

26:11.611 --> 26:13.863
[water splashing]

26:19.703 --> 26:21.663
[buzzing, crackling]

26:23.540 --> 26:24.916
What is this game?

26:26.960 --> 26:28.586
[phone chiming]

26:28.670 --> 26:31.006
[announcer] Game entry is now closed.

26:31.089 --> 26:33.842
There are seven participants.

26:33.925 --> 26:35.510
The game is about to commence.

26:35.593 --> 26:36.928
[phones chime]

26:37.554 --> 26:40.056
Difficulty, Four of Diamonds.

26:40.140 --> 26:40.974
GAME DIFFICULTY

26:41.057 --> 26:43.435
This is the last Diamond we need.

26:43.518 --> 26:44.728
[electricity crackling]

26:44.811 --> 26:47.731
[announcer] Game, "Light Bulb".

26:48.857 --> 26:49.733
[Tatta] "Light bulb"?

26:50.567 --> 26:52.402
OPEN AND CLOSE FREELY

26:55.697 --> 26:58.033
- [phone chimes]
- [announcer] Game play challenge.

26:58.116 --> 27:00.827
- Which switch turns the light bulb on?
- [upbeat music]

27:03.705 --> 27:05.582
WHICH SWITCH TURNS ON THE LIGHT BULB?

27:05.665 --> 27:07.000
[announcer] Rule one.

27:08.418 --> 27:14.049
Only one of the switches, A, B, or C,
will turn the light bulb on.

27:15.842 --> 27:17.010
Rule two.

27:17.761 --> 27:22.349
You only have one chance
to leave the door open

27:22.432 --> 27:24.351
while flipping a switch.

27:27.437 --> 27:29.522
When the door is closed,

27:29.606 --> 27:33.276
you may flip any switch
or as many as you like.

27:34.903 --> 27:36.112
Rule three.

27:37.113 --> 27:41.076
If a player is in the room
and the switch is flipped on,

27:41.785 --> 27:46.289
the door to the room will be locked
and cannot be reopened.

27:47.957 --> 27:51.878
Participants have only one chance
to answer as a group.

27:51.961 --> 27:57.300
The game is cleared when you determine
which switch turns the light bulb on.

27:57.384 --> 27:59.386
As the water level rises,

27:59.469 --> 28:02.180
should water touch
the hanging electrical wires,

28:02.263 --> 28:04.307
it is game over.

28:05.058 --> 28:06.267
Electrical wires?

28:07.102 --> 28:08.728
- [explosion]
- [girl groans]

28:12.190 --> 28:14.234
And those would be the electrical wires.

28:15.693 --> 28:17.237
Remember, don't touch.

28:19.030 --> 28:20.490
The water level is rising!

28:21.157 --> 28:23.535
If it gets high enough, we'll all die.

28:23.618 --> 28:26.955
Okay, listen! We just need to know
which switch turns on the light.

28:27.038 --> 28:30.083
I'll go into the room first,
we'll take turns!

28:30.166 --> 28:32.210
If you go in, the door won't close!

28:32.293 --> 28:33.837
Let's see…

28:33.920 --> 28:36.631
And you can only try once
with the door open.

28:36.714 --> 28:39.592
[Tatta] But if we close the door,
it doesn't make sense to flip a switch.

28:39.676 --> 28:40.927
We won't know if the light's on!

28:41.010 --> 28:44.681
Yes, but suppose we flip the A switch
with the door open,

28:44.764 --> 28:46.474
but the light bulb doesn't light.

28:46.558 --> 28:49.269
Then we'll only know
that it's not the A switch.

28:49.352 --> 28:51.020
Well, have you got a better idea?

28:53.148 --> 28:56.317
I say that you… you flip the A switch
with the door open.

28:56.401 --> 28:58.069
[Kuina]
And if the light bulb doesn't go on?

28:58.153 --> 29:01.197
If the light bulb turns on,
then it's switch A. If not, it's B or C.

29:01.281 --> 29:03.450
That way we've got a 50 percent chance!

29:03.533 --> 29:05.243
66 percent.

29:06.703 --> 29:08.246
You sure? It should be 50 percent.

29:08.830 --> 29:11.040
Gotta tell you,
I'm not following any of this.

29:11.624 --> 29:13.501
What will you do, Arisu?

29:16.087 --> 29:17.464
There's no other choice.

29:18.214 --> 29:20.550
All right, with the door open,
I'll flip the switch!

29:20.633 --> 29:21.968
If the light bulb doesn't light,

29:22.051 --> 29:24.304
we'll be left with choosing
between the other two switches.

29:24.387 --> 29:25.722
So it's a shot in the dark?

29:26.723 --> 29:29.392
- It's all I've got.
- With seven people's lives.

29:33.354 --> 29:34.647
Sorry, six.

29:35.440 --> 29:38.485
Ann, if you know how to solve this,
then tell us!

29:38.568 --> 29:41.780
I told you, Arisu. We are testing you.

29:43.323 --> 29:45.992
Give me a break!
Don't drag me into some rookie test.

29:46.075 --> 29:47.202
Gonna give up?

29:47.285 --> 29:50.288
Well, I give up. Just tell me the answer!

29:52.248 --> 29:54.250
We'll die! Tell him!

29:54.334 --> 29:56.461
- [electricity crackles]
- The answer!

29:57.420 --> 30:00.131
Arisu, just do it before it's too late!

30:01.132 --> 30:02.759
I don't know how!

30:03.635 --> 30:06.346
Think it through, Arisu.

30:06.429 --> 30:08.431
[tense music]

30:11.142 --> 30:13.645
- Go on, go on!
- What are you waiting for?

30:22.237 --> 30:24.239
[announcer] You only have one chance

30:24.322 --> 30:27.075
- to leave the door open while…
- [Ann] What would happen

30:27.158 --> 30:29.536
if you flip the A switch
with the door open,

30:29.619 --> 30:31.329
but the light bulb doesn't light?

30:31.412 --> 30:34.374
[Tatta] If the light bulb turns on,
then it's switch A. If not, it's B or C!

30:34.457 --> 30:38.336
[announcer] If the door is closed,
you may flip any switch.

30:39.671 --> 30:41.005
Close the door.

30:41.089 --> 30:42.131
Huh?

30:42.966 --> 30:45.343
Close the door! Hurry!

30:45.844 --> 30:48.680
I'd do what he says.
Otherwise, we're dead.

30:53.268 --> 30:55.645
[both grunt]

31:00.984 --> 31:01.943
Don't move!

31:02.819 --> 31:04.612
But why not?

31:04.696 --> 31:06.114
What are you doing?

31:10.743 --> 31:13.162
[electricity buzzing]

31:21.004 --> 31:22.171
Hurry up!

31:24.257 --> 31:25.300
Open it!

31:25.383 --> 31:27.385
[tense music]

31:35.810 --> 31:37.186
Hurry up!

31:38.855 --> 31:40.857
[suspenseful music]

31:43.109 --> 31:44.527
It didn't light!

31:44.611 --> 31:46.821
Kuina! Go in and touch it!

31:46.905 --> 31:47.989
Huh?

31:48.072 --> 31:50.533
Go touch the bulb! Our time's running out.

31:53.745 --> 31:55.830
Get us out! Get us out!

31:57.832 --> 31:59.042
It's hot!

31:59.626 --> 32:01.502
- The answer is switch A--
- Switch A!

32:02.879 --> 32:04.005
[machine rumbles]

32:05.256 --> 32:08.259
[powering down]

32:16.184 --> 32:18.353
[breathes shakily]

32:20.146 --> 32:21.272
[phone chiming]

32:21.356 --> 32:25.109
[announcer] Game cleared. Congratulations.

32:25.693 --> 32:30.323
[breathing heavily]

32:33.159 --> 32:34.702
The light bulb is incandescent.

32:34.786 --> 32:37.205
It stayed hot because it was on.

32:37.288 --> 32:39.415
If it was cold, it wasn't on.

32:39.499 --> 32:41.918
I threw the switch to confirm it.

32:42.502 --> 32:46.422
That raised the odds
from 66 percent to 100 percent.

32:48.257 --> 32:49.384
[pants]

32:50.176 --> 32:53.304
[sighs]
It should've been 50 percent.

32:53.888 --> 32:55.431
I don't care anymore.

32:55.515 --> 32:57.517
[upbeat music playing]

32:57.600 --> 32:58.643
[cheering]

32:59.227 --> 33:03.147
♪ Hey, whatcha say? We got to move ♪

33:03.231 --> 33:06.359
♪ What's taking so long ♪

33:06.442 --> 33:10.697
♪ Hey, I'll get my ride
That shiny shoes ♪

33:10.780 --> 33:13.241
♪ The heat's turning on ♪

33:13.908 --> 33:16.703
♪ So amazing ♪

33:17.203 --> 33:19.956
♪ I got a flow of good things ♪

33:21.165 --> 33:23.668
♪ Babe, make a wish ♪

33:23.751 --> 33:25.503
[Usagi pants]

33:27.296 --> 33:28.423
You made it.

33:29.132 --> 33:30.091
Mm-hm.

33:35.930 --> 33:38.224
Ann knew the answer the whole time.

33:41.352 --> 33:43.813
They were… testing me.

33:45.148 --> 33:47.483
When in Rome, do as the Romans do, right?

33:52.822 --> 33:53.906
Is she your girlfriend?

33:53.990 --> 33:56.826
What? No, I'm not.

33:57.410 --> 33:59.704
If you two like each other,
why not hook up?

34:00.455 --> 34:02.874
You guys could die tomorrow.

34:02.957 --> 34:04.208
What's it to you?

34:04.292 --> 34:06.127
[Kuina]
You should live while you're alive.

34:10.381 --> 34:12.383
My mother is stuck in a hospital.

34:13.384 --> 34:16.137
She can't even go to the toilet
by herself.

34:16.679 --> 34:18.139
And I wound up here.

34:19.515 --> 34:21.434
That's why I need to survive and go home.

34:22.060 --> 34:24.854
And that's the reason I quit smoking.

34:25.897 --> 34:28.316
Back in the day, I couldn't stop smoking.

34:29.442 --> 34:31.778
But to survive the game,
you need to stay healthy.

34:33.946 --> 34:36.866
[Kuina] I absolutely need to survive
and go back to my other world.

34:36.949 --> 34:40.411
- [clanging in distance]
- [Niragi] Hey! Stop that crap music.

34:40.495 --> 34:42.038
[music stops]

34:48.211 --> 34:50.129
[crowd murmuring]

34:52.256 --> 34:54.759
[Kuina]
They're the militant corps at the Beach.

34:55.426 --> 34:57.887
If you want to live in peace here,

34:57.970 --> 34:59.889
then do not mess with them.

35:03.392 --> 35:06.312
[Kuina] General Aguni is
an ex-Special Forces officer.

35:06.395 --> 35:08.689
He controls all of the weapons
at the beach.

35:10.483 --> 35:12.944
The person who commands the beach
right now

35:13.027 --> 35:15.363
is the number one Hatter and his lackeys.

35:16.906 --> 35:19.659
As well as the militants led by Aguni.

35:20.910 --> 35:24.163
Right now, law and order at the Beach is
very fragile.

35:24.247 --> 35:27.166
Both of these groups could clash
at any time.

35:37.969 --> 35:39.262
Where's your friend?

35:40.138 --> 35:42.140
[slow tense music]

35:46.394 --> 35:48.146
Oh, yeah? He's dead?

35:49.272 --> 35:50.523
Too bad.

35:51.399 --> 35:53.359
Yet someone like you still lives.

35:54.569 --> 35:56.112
You know each other?

36:01.159 --> 36:01.993
Hey.

36:03.119 --> 36:04.537
Bring the woman.

36:05.371 --> 36:06.664
You got it.

36:07.790 --> 36:10.001
- Whoa!
- You crazy? Don't get involved.

36:11.085 --> 36:13.546
My boss says to bring you to him.

36:15.590 --> 36:16.799
Get up.

36:17.425 --> 36:18.467
[Arisu] Leave her.

36:20.178 --> 36:22.972
Are you a tough guy?
What should I do with him?

36:23.556 --> 36:26.267
Break both his legs
so he dies in the next game.

36:26.934 --> 36:28.519
Good one. Hey!

36:28.603 --> 36:30.229
Take the woman.

36:31.105 --> 36:32.732
And you, come with me.

36:34.108 --> 36:35.359
[Niragi] Come on, let's go.

36:38.404 --> 36:39.405
Huh?

36:42.241 --> 36:43.784
Aw.

36:45.244 --> 36:46.537
[Hatter] Is there a problem?

36:52.376 --> 36:55.421
[Aguni] Back off, Hatter.
This is none of your business.

36:57.048 --> 36:59.008
But this business is mine.

36:59.926 --> 37:04.013
I am the Beach's leader.
What I say is the law here.

37:06.474 --> 37:08.434
And I'm saying…

37:09.101 --> 37:13.397
that you will keep your hands
off the newcomers, Aguni.

37:21.197 --> 37:22.448
Niragi?

37:23.324 --> 37:24.825
[sighs, clicks tongue]

37:24.909 --> 37:27.912
The only boss I have is the general.

37:36.963 --> 37:39.423
[Hatter] Then I will ask the general.

37:43.427 --> 37:45.930
Who do you think is your boss, then,

37:46.514 --> 37:47.765
Aguni?

37:57.316 --> 37:59.860
[tense music]

38:03.614 --> 38:05.199
I know it is you.

38:13.416 --> 38:15.251
Shower once in a while.

38:16.002 --> 38:18.796
Executive members!
Meeting in the conference room.

38:25.428 --> 38:27.638
Arisu, you too.

38:29.807 --> 38:32.393
Ann told me you have potential.

38:33.728 --> 38:34.770
Come with us.

38:42.945 --> 38:43.988
I better go.

38:58.169 --> 38:59.045
So?

38:59.670 --> 39:01.797
How was he? Is he good?

39:03.883 --> 39:05.134
He was great.

39:06.093 --> 39:07.595
[overlapping chatter]

39:07.678 --> 39:09.347
[Hatter]
All right, let's start the meeting.

39:09.430 --> 39:12.099
If you're not an executive member,
leave the room.

39:12.183 --> 39:14.018
[overlapping chatter]

39:20.107 --> 39:20.941
[door closes]

39:33.287 --> 39:34.413
Hi.

39:34.497 --> 39:37.041
[Mira] We took the Two of Spades.

39:38.209 --> 39:41.212
Six of Spades. Four of Diamonds.

39:41.712 --> 39:43.798
And the Two of Clubs.

39:45.216 --> 39:49.595
So far, the existence of any face cards
has not been confirmed.

39:50.429 --> 39:51.847
If there are no face cards,

39:51.931 --> 39:53.891
then only the Ten of Hearts remains.

39:55.267 --> 39:56.936
[Mira] The Ten of Hearts.

39:57.645 --> 40:00.398
It hasn't appeared in any game yet.

40:00.481 --> 40:02.483
[ominous music]

40:05.486 --> 40:07.488
[Ann]
If the Ten of Hearts hasn't appeared yet,

40:08.072 --> 40:10.366
then maybe there's a reason for it.

40:11.700 --> 40:12.993
Perhaps it's not in Tokyo.

40:13.828 --> 40:16.539
No game arena has been found
outside the 23 districts.

40:16.622 --> 40:19.125
That only means
we haven't searched far enough.

40:19.208 --> 40:20.668
We're not changing the plan.

40:22.670 --> 40:26.048
The search for the other game arenas
in Tokyo will continue.

40:26.132 --> 40:27.591
Keep an eye on visa expirations.

40:27.675 --> 40:29.760
Let's wait for the Ten of Hearts
to show up.

40:31.595 --> 40:34.306
My visa needs to be reissued soon.

40:41.897 --> 40:43.399
Respectfully,

40:44.024 --> 40:46.360
there is a way to earn a visa.

40:47.361 --> 40:48.237
Oh?

40:50.489 --> 40:51.615
A Hearts game…

40:52.491 --> 40:55.995
is a game that plays
with people's minds and emotions.

40:57.204 --> 40:59.540
We use a decoy we know will die

41:00.291 --> 41:02.751
and fix the game so that you survive.

41:05.254 --> 41:08.299
Arisu cleared the Seven of Hearts game.

41:09.133 --> 41:10.718
I guess that means…

41:11.594 --> 41:14.930
If he can do it, then anyone can!

41:16.599 --> 41:19.351
Arisu, you cleared the Seven of Hearts?

41:19.435 --> 41:21.228
Can you give us any advice?

41:22.229 --> 41:24.023
[laughs]

41:26.484 --> 41:29.695
There's no way to predict
when a Hearts game may appear.

41:30.196 --> 41:33.324
Don't forget, we only find out
what the game is

41:33.407 --> 41:35.159
after registration closes.

41:35.242 --> 41:38.746
True, but the theory of probability
should help us determine the arena.

41:38.829 --> 41:39.705
[thuds]

41:40.372 --> 41:43.083
I don't need pretentious theories.

41:44.752 --> 41:46.879
I will participate in the next game.

41:47.421 --> 41:49.882
[Hatter]
I don't care if it's a Heart or a Spade.

41:49.965 --> 41:52.593
I can clear them all!

41:53.594 --> 41:56.305
And I'll be there
when the Ten of Hearts appears.

41:57.139 --> 42:00.684
The cards are on the table.
Our day of departure is near!

42:02.811 --> 42:06.649
Executives, you're in charge
while I'm away.

42:08.817 --> 42:09.777
[Hatter claps]

42:09.860 --> 42:10.945
Meeting adjourned!

42:16.742 --> 42:20.704
[opera music playing]

42:31.715 --> 42:33.008
[moans]

42:35.135 --> 42:38.347
[women giggle]

42:38.430 --> 42:41.058
[opera music continues playing]

42:45.354 --> 42:47.439
[smooching]

42:48.649 --> 42:50.025
[slurps]

42:54.071 --> 42:55.114
[moans]

42:55.197 --> 42:56.240
Mwah.

42:58.033 --> 43:00.202
Arisu, have a drink.

43:05.374 --> 43:09.628
I always like to have a little fun
before a game.

43:14.133 --> 43:17.219
[laughing]

43:18.387 --> 43:20.681
What do you think? That I'd poison you?

43:20.764 --> 43:22.308
[women giggling]

43:24.059 --> 43:25.269
[slurps]

43:26.103 --> 43:27.021
Hmm?

43:27.813 --> 43:28.856
Mm.

43:30.065 --> 43:31.358
Is that proof enough?

43:31.859 --> 43:34.278
You really don't trust me, do you?

43:39.074 --> 43:42.745
You're a cautious young man. I like that.

43:44.246 --> 43:46.415
What did you use to do
in the normal world?

43:49.043 --> 43:52.588
- Nothing.
- Mmm. Nerd, yeah?

43:55.007 --> 43:59.720
Me? I used to run
a men's club in Kabukicho.

44:00.846 --> 44:03.932
"Beach" was its name.

44:04.016 --> 44:05.434
Ever hear of it?

44:05.976 --> 44:07.269
[laughs]

44:07.353 --> 44:09.563
It was the place to go!

44:09.647 --> 44:13.484
♪ Beach, Beach, come and bring a friend
It's utopia, Beach! ♪

44:13.567 --> 44:15.277
[laughs]

44:18.614 --> 44:21.367
That radio commercial was playing
all the time.

44:22.493 --> 44:24.036
I was gaming all the time.

44:24.119 --> 44:25.120
Ah.

44:34.421 --> 44:35.547
What I wanted…

44:38.550 --> 44:41.095
was to be the best in Kabukicho.

44:43.263 --> 44:45.349
So desperate.

44:54.400 --> 44:56.819
My men and I were always saying,

44:57.528 --> 45:00.989
[inhales sharply]
"We're gonna take over this city!"

45:08.372 --> 45:10.124
As a host, it's all over.

45:11.959 --> 45:14.503
If you're looked down on
by your customers,

45:16.463 --> 45:18.632
then you go back home alone.

45:20.843 --> 45:25.556
"You can never, ever,
stop being proud of yourself."

45:27.724 --> 45:30.936
That's what I always said to my men.

45:35.315 --> 45:37.484
Even so…
[sniffs]

45:41.155 --> 45:43.782
…one of my men lost his pride one night.

45:48.287 --> 45:49.413
He went home…

45:53.459 --> 45:54.918
and hanged himself.

46:04.553 --> 46:06.805
They all left me.
[sniffs]

46:11.727 --> 46:12.936
I wanted…

46:16.773 --> 46:19.526
I wanted to rule the place with them.

46:23.447 --> 46:24.656
[sniffs]

46:26.909 --> 46:28.619
Now that I think about it,

46:31.246 --> 46:34.082
his death was a necessary evil.

46:37.252 --> 46:39.630
You see, it made me that much stronger.

46:42.007 --> 46:43.383
Stronger?

46:47.387 --> 46:49.598
[Hatter] At this new Beach,

46:50.516 --> 46:53.977
all the players are devoted to me.

46:54.061 --> 46:56.021
They would die for me!

46:58.815 --> 47:01.735
They have made me their number one.

47:04.738 --> 47:07.783
When I finally escape from this country,

47:07.866 --> 47:09.993
I will be their hero!

47:14.248 --> 47:16.250
The hero, Hatter.

47:32.558 --> 47:34.434
But to have a hero,

47:35.769 --> 47:37.688
you need to have a tragedy.

47:46.822 --> 47:48.824
- [Hatter] To the new Beach.
- [glasses clink]

47:55.872 --> 47:58.667
- [glass thuds]
- [exhales heavily]

48:03.005 --> 48:06.174
[opera music intensifies]

48:19.521 --> 48:21.857
[opera music continues]

48:45.672 --> 48:47.674
[closing theme music]
